// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ADD THIS to your Firestore security rules in the Firebase console:
//   Firebase console → Firestore Database → Rules
// Place the `match /recommendations/...` block INSIDE your existing
//   `match /databases/{database}/documents { ... }` block, alongside the
//   rules you already have for `users` and `books`, then click Publish.
//
// This app has no Firebase Auth (users are picked from a list), so — like the
// rest of the app — these rules are open. They exist only to stop Firestore's
// default-deny from blocking the recommendations feature. If you later add
// real auth, tighten these to the request.auth.uid checks from the spec.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

match /recommendations/{id} {
  allow read, write: if true;
}
